# moments.dat, the angular polynomial of each moment of the LPT final integral (read by lpt_tables.py).
# Generated by python -m pt_autogen regenerate, pt_autogen 2.1 (2026-11-10): matrix table headers.
# Identity: with mu_K = Khat.qhat, mu_x = e_x.qhat (e_x = (khat - c Khat)/s), mu_y the third component and the
#   polynomial P_j = sum over the lines of moment j of coef A_mu^pAm B_mu^pBm mu_K^a mu_x^b mu_y^by (degree n), the
#   angular integral of moment j is
#     M_j = (-i)^(n mod 2) int dOmega/(4 pi) e^(i k.q) e^(B mu_K^2) P_j = sum_L j_L(kq) C_L^j,
#   with B = -(1/2) K^2 Y_lin_lt, A_mu = (1 + f) mu / Kfac, B_mu = sqrt(1 - mu^2) / Kfac, n.qhat = A_mu mu_K - B_mu mu_x
#   and the Legendre coefficients C_L^j of angular.dat.
# Order: the moments in declaration order (lpt_model.DENSITY_MOMENTS, the moment index of the runtime), within a moment
#   the terms in declaration order.
# Counts: 9 moments, 14 lines.
# Coefficients: integers.
# columns: moment coef pAm pBm a b by
MQ0       1  0 0  0 0 0
MQ1       1  0 0  1 0 0
MQ2       1  0 0  2 0 0
MQ3       1  0 0  3 0 0
MQ4       1  0 0  4 0 0
NQ1       1  1 0  1 0 0
NQ1      -1  0 1  0 1 0
NQ2       1  2 0  2 0 0
NQ2      -2  1 1  1 1 0
NQ2       1  0 2  0 2 0
MQ1NQ1    1  1 0  2 0 0
MQ1NQ1   -1  0 1  1 1 0
MQ2NQ1    1  1 0  3 0 0
MQ2NQ1   -1  0 1  2 1 0
